msgid "Priced groups making up the trip cost, in the order the cart holds them. `price_category` is the per-traveler-category pricing and leads the list; the rest are what add-ons priced, such as `extra_service` or `accommodation`. Cart-level fees and discounts are not part of this resource."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:967
msgid "Line item group key, e.g. `price_category` or `extra_service`. A slug, not a numeric ID."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:969
msgid "Priced rows inside this group."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:974
msgid "Row ID: the ID of the catalogue entry the row was booked from, or one generated for a row typed by hand. The price category ID on a `price_category` row."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:975
msgid "Row label, e.g. `Adult` on a `price_category` row."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:977
msgid "Quantity booked for this row; travelers, on a `price_category` row."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:981
msgid "Unit price for this row at the time of booking."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:984
msgid "Row total: quantity times price. Negative for a discount."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:992
msgid "Travelers on this trip, in booking order; the first is the lead traveler. Keys are not fixed: every key except `cat_id` and `cat_label` is a checkout form field, so the set depends on which traveler fields the site collects and on anything add-ons inject through `wp_travel_engine_traveller_info_fields_display` and `wp_travel_engine_lead_traveller_info_fields_display`. Commonly present are `title`, `fname`, `lname`, `email`, `phone`, `country`, `address`, `city`, `postcode`, `passport` and `dob`, but none of them is guaranteed. A file field holds its files as `{ id, name, mime, url }` objects when one booking is read, and its attachment IDs in a list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:999
msgid "Price category ID this traveler was booked under. Always present: it is resolved from cart info rather than submitted on the form."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1003
msgid "Price category label, e.g. `Adult`. Always present, for the same reason as `cat_id`."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1007
msgid "Where this traveler is collected from, when they are. Optional: absent on a traveler without a pickup."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1011
msgid "Pickup location, as the trip lists it or as the operator named it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1028
msgid "Seat availability for this trip on its booked date, computed per request and never stored. Absent when the trip or package has been deleted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1033
msgid "Date the availability was computed for, as `Y-m-d`."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1037
msgid "Seat state. `past` is a departure that has already gone; `unknown` means it could not be determined."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1042
msgid "True when neither the package nor the trip caps participants."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1046
msgid "Seats the package allows on this date. Null when capacity is uncapped."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1050
msgid "Capacity minus the pax of every other booking on this date. This booking is excluded, so it never counts against itself. Negative means oversold."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1054
msgid "Travelers this booking itself holds on the date."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1063
msgid "Amounts taken off the booking, such as a coupon. Named by the cart in the same way a fee is, so a discount an add-on registered reads like the coupon core applies. Held against the cart rather than a trip, since one coupon covers the whole booking. Write these back through the matching `discounts` of the update endpoint, which takes rows of this same shape."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1071
msgid "Name the cart deducts this under, e.g. `coupon`. This is what a write passes back as `discount.slug`."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1075
msgid "Label as it was applied, e.g. the coupon code."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1079
msgid "What the deduction is for, as the cart recorded it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1083
msgid "How the deduction is worked out: a share of the subtotal, or a set amount."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1088
msgid "The rate, when the deduction is a percentage. Zero on a fixed one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1092
msgid "What the deduction came to, in the booking currency."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1096
msgid "Whether the terms were typed by hand rather than taken from a coupon. Sent back on a write so a row read from here is not mistaken for the coupon its name matches."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1103
msgid "Billing details for whoever paid. `fname`, `lname` and `email` are always collected; every other key is a billing checkout field the site has enabled, extendable through `wp_travel_engine_booking_fields_display`, so custom fields appear here under their own keys. A file field holds its files as `{ id, name, mime, url }` objects when one booking is read, and its attachment IDs in a list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1110
msgid "First name. Always collected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1114
msgid "Last name. Always collected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1118
msgid "Email address the booking confirmation is sent to. Empty on an abandoned booking that never reached the billing step, so this is not validated as an email on read."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1124
msgid "Emergency contact for the booking. Keys are not fixed: they are the emergency-contact checkout fields the site collects, extendable through `wp_travel_engine_emergency_contact_fields_display`. Commonly present are `fname`, `lname`, `phone`, `country` and `relation`, but none of them is guaranteed. A file field holds its files as `{ id, name, mime, url }` objects when one booking is read, and its attachment IDs in a list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1131
msgid "Payment records against this booking, oldest first. A deposit booking has several."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1139
msgid "Payment post ID."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1143
msgid "Gateway name for display, e.g. `PayPal`."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1147
msgid "Gateway slug the payment was taken through, e.g. `paypal`, `stripe`, `bank_transfer`."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1151
msgid "Transaction date, as `Y-m-d H:i`. Set by the gateway or the operator; a payment carrying none reports the date its record was opened, so this is never empty."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1155
msgid "Where the payment came from: `checkout` for one the customer made, `admin` for one recorded in wp-admin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1160
msgid "Whether the record is a request the customer has yet to settle rather than money already taken. Stays true once it is paid - what became of the request is `status`."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1164
msgid "URL the customer settles this payment through. Empty unless `is_payment_request` is true, once the payment is completed, and on a payment whose booking cannot be resolved."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1168
msgid "Raw payment status slug as the gateway reported it, e.g. `completed`, `capture`, `voucher-awaiting`. Deliberately unconstrained: the vocabulary is merged from four status-group helpers and extended through `wp_travel_engine_payment_status_options`, so gateways and add-ons add to it. Kept for fidelity and reconciliation — several slugs collapse onto one label, so the raw value cannot be recovered from a label. Use `status_type` to display it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1172
msgid "Gateway transaction reference, for reconciliation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1176
msgid "Currency the payment was taken in. May differ from the booking currency when the gateway settled in another."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1180
msgid "Amount this payment settled."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1184
msgid "Whether `deposit_value` is a share of the balance due or a set amount. Empty on a payment recorded before this was kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1188
msgid "The figure the deposit was worked out from, as it was entered."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1192
msgid "Amount this payment is for, before the fees it carries."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1196
msgid "Amount refunded from this payment."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1200
msgid "Operator note recorded against this payment. Never shown to the customer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1204
msgid "What `paid_amount` was made up of, keyed by the name the cart charged each fee under - so an add-on fee appears beside `booking_fee` and `tax` without being named here. `deposit` is derived, the amount less every fee, so the parts always sum back to `paid_amount`. A payment taken before the split was recorded reports zero for each fee and the whole amount as `deposit`."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1210
msgid "What the payment covered before fee and tax."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1215
msgid "Booking fee this payment carried."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1219
msgid "Tax this payment carried. Distinct from the tax on the whole booking, which a booking settled in several payments splits across them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1228
msgid "Notes attached to the booking: the note the customer left at checkout, and any notes staff have added since. `type` and `content` are writable; `date` and `author` are stamped by the server."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1235
msgid "Identifier for the note, unique within the booking. `customer` for the checkout note, which is one per booking; an internal note carries its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1239
msgid "Who the note came from. A customer note is visible to the customer; an admin note is internal."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1244
msgid "Note text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1247
msgid "When the note was added, as `Y-m-d H:i:s`."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1248
msgid "Display name of whoever added the note. Empty for a customer note."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1253
msgid "What has happened to the booking, newest first. Core records the edits made through this endpoint; `wptravelengine_booking_activities` may add to that list or replace it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1262
msgid "Identifier for the entry, unique within the booking."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1266
msgid "What kind of event it was, which decides the icon the client draws: `payment`, `refund`, `document`, `document_shared`, `traveler`, `addon` or `message`. Anything else renders as a plain entry, so an add-on may report its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1270
msgid "Which filter the entry falls under. Core files one under `payments`, `bookings` for the status and the date it was placed, `discounts`, `travelers` for billing, contacts and traveler details, `addons` for priced rows other than a traveler category, or `misc`. Not a closed set: an add-on may file its own, and anything the client does not know a filter for reads as `misc`."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1274
msgid "Who the entry is attributed to, which decides the badge."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1279
msgid "Display name for whoever acted, e.g. a traveler name, `You`, `System`."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1283
msgid "When it happened, as `Y-m-d H:i:s`."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1287
msgid "What happened, in a sentence, already translated."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1294
msgid "Changes the traveler has asked for — a date move, a cancellation — newest first. Core stores none of its own: the list is whatever `wptravelengine_booking_traveler_requests` supplies, so it is empty unless an add-on fills it. Nothing here is applied automatically; each entry is a note for staff to act on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1303
msgid "Identifier for the request, unique within the booking."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1307
msgid "What is being asked for. `date_change` and `cancellation` are what core names; an add-on may report others, so treat an unknown type as a plain request."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1311
msgid "One-line heading for the request, already translated."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1315
msgid "When the traveler submitted it, as `Y-m-d H:i:s`."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1319
msgid "Extra context shown beside the date, e.g. `130 days before departure`. Empty when there is none."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1323
msgid "What the request amounts to, in a sentence."
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/Core/Controllers/RestAPI/V2/Booking.php:1327
